Article 19 A labor contract shall be concluded in written form and shall contain the following clauses:
(1) The term of the labor contract;
(2) The work content;
(3) Labor protection and labor conditions;
(4) Labor remuneration;
(5) Labor discipline;
(6) The conditions for the termination of the labor contract;
(7) The liability for breach of the labor contract.
In addition to the essential clauses specified in the preceding paragraph, the parties may negotiate and agree upon other contents.

Article 25 The employer may rescind the labor contract if the worker is in any of the following circumstances:
(1) Being proved not up to the recruitment requirements during the probation period;
(2) Seriously violating labor discipline or the rules and regulations of the employer;
(3) Committing serious dereliction of duty or engaging in malpractices for personal gain, causing major damage to the interests of the employer;
(4) Being investigated for criminal liability according to law.

Article 26 The employer may rescind the labor contract in any of the following circumstances, but shall notify the worker in writing 30 days in advance:
(1) After the expiration of the medical treatment period, the worker is unable to engage in the original work nor in any other work arranged by the employer due to illness or non-work-related injury;
(2) The worker is incompetent for his/her job, and remains incompetent after receiving training or adjusting his/her post;
(3) The objective conditions taken as the basis for the conclusion of the contract have undergone major changes, rendering the original labor contract unenforceable, and the parties fail to reach an agreement on the modification of the labor contract through consultation.

Article 29 The employer shall not rescind the labor contract in accordance with the provisions of Articles 26 and 27 of this Law if the worker is in any of the following circumstances:
(1) Having contracted an occupational disease or suffered a work-related injury and being confirmed to have lost or partially lost the ability to work;
(2) Suffering from an illness or injury and being within the prescribed medical treatment period;
(3) Being a female employee in her pregnancy, puerperal period, or nursing period;
(4) Other circumstances provided for by laws, administrative regulations.

Article 32 The worker may notify the employer at any time to rescind the labor contract in any of the following circumstances:
(1) During the probation period;
(2) The employer compels the worker to work by violence, threats or illegal restriction of personal freedom;
(3) The employer fails to pay labor remuneration or provide working conditions as agreed in the labor contract.

Article 40 The employer shall arrange for its workers to take vacations during the following festivals according to law:
(1) New Year's Day;
(2) The Spring Festival;
(3) International Labor Day;
(4) National Day;
(5) Other holidays provided for by laws and regulations.

Article 42 Under any of the following circumstances, the extension of working hours shall not be subject to the restrictions provided in Article 41 of this Law:
(1) Where emergency handling is needed in the event of natural disasters, accidents or other reasons that threaten the life, health and property safety of workers;
(2) Where breakdowns occur in production equipment, transportation lines or public facilities, affecting production and public interests, and urgent repairs must be carried out;
(3) Other circumstances as provided by laws and administrative regulations.

Article 44 Under any of the following circumstances, the employer shall pay the workers remuneration higher than their normal wages according to the following standards:
(1) Where the workers are arranged to extend their working hours, the remuneration shall be no less than 150 percent of their wages;
(2) Where the workers are arranged to work on rest days and no compensatory time off can be arranged, the remuneration shall be no less than 200 percent of their wages;
(3) Where the workers are arranged to work on statutory holidays, the remuneration shall be no less than 300 percent of their wages.

Article 49 The following factors shall be comprehensively taken into account in determining and adjusting the minimum wage standard:
(1) The minimum living expenses of the workers themselves and the average number of dependants;
(2) The average social wage level;
(3) The labor productivity;
(4) The employment situation;
(5) The differences in economic development levels among regions.

Article 73 Workers shall, under the following circumstances, enjoy social insurance benefits according to law:
(1) Retirement;
(2) Illness or injury;
(3) Work-related disability or occupational disease;
(4) Unemployment;
(5) Childbirth.
After the death of a worker, his or her surviving family members shall enjoy survivors' benefits according to law.
The conditions and standards for workers to enjoy social insurance benefits shall be prescribed by laws and regulations.
The social insurance benefits that workers enjoy must be paid in full and on time.

Article 91 Where an employing unit commits any of the following acts infringing upon the legitimate rights and interests of workers, the labor administrative department shall order it to pay the workers' wages or economic compensation, and may order it to pay compensation:
(1) docking or unjustifiably delaying the payment of workers' wages;
(2) refusing to pay workers the remuneration for extended working hours;
(3) paying workers wages below the local minimum wage standard;
(4) failing to provide workers with economic compensation in accordance with the provisions of this Law after rescinding a labor contract.

Article 96 Where an employing unit commits any of the following acts, the public security organ shall impose on the persons responsible a detention of not more than fifteen days, a fine, or a warning; if the act constitutes a crime, the persons responsible shall be investigated for criminal liability according to law:
(1) forcing labor by means of violence, threats, or illegally restricting personal freedom;
(2) insulting, subjecting workers to corporal punishment, beating, illegally searching, or detaining workers.
